#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Lemma]
#title[Class Formula]

Let $G$ be a finite #local("00DL")[group] with an action $X : B G -> "1-Type"$,
then the groupoid cardinality of the action type computes to
$
  |X_(h G)| = (|X("sh"_G)|)/(|U G|).
$

#proof[
  We begin by characterizing the connected components of $X_(h G)$.
  Define the $G$-set $overline(X) : B G -> "Set"$ by $overline(X)(u) :-= ||X(u)||_0$.
  By the #link("00HF")[HoTT Book, Theorem 7.3.9], we have that
  $||X_(h G)||_0 ~= ||overline(X)_(h G)||_0$.
  Since $overline(X)$ acts on a set, by #link("00D6")[the Symmetry Book, Lemma 5.4.4]
  $|| overline(X)_(h G)||_0 ~= overline(X) slash G$
  So the connceted components of $X_(h G)$ are precisely the orbits of the action $overline(X)$.
  $
    ||X_(h G)||_0 ~= overline(X) slash G 
  $


  We now go on to identify the automorphisms of $X_(h G)$. Observe that
  $
    U "Aut"_X_(h G) ("sh"_G, x) -=& ( "sh"_G, x) =_X_(h G) ("sh"_G, x)\
    ~=& sum_(g : U G) (g * x = x)\
    ~=& sum_(g : U G) (g * x = x) xx ||g* x = x||_(-1)\
    ~=& sum_((g,!) : sum_(g : U G) ||g * x = x||_(-1) ) (g * x = x) \
  $
]
#local("00ID")[TODO] : therefor
$
  |U "Aut"_X_(h G)("sh"_G, x)| = | sum_(g : U G) ||g * x = x||_(-1)| * | U "Aut"_X("sh"_G) (x)|
$

